d.page('Review 1','Introduction and requirements');d.section('I  Acknowledgement','Team 1 presents the Maison Rue project as an application of web interface development, business workflow design and relational data management. Academic attribution and named contributions are completed in the project team records.');d.section('II  Introduction',intro[1][2]);d.section('III  Synopsis','Maison Rue combines a customer fashion storefront with operational and administrative portals. Its scope extends from product discovery and variant selection to fulfilment, physical return inspection and reporting.');d.section('IV  Problem definition','Customers need consistent information about fit, materials, availability and after sales decisions. Staff need traceable order and stock workflows. Administrators need controlled employee access, campaign tools and reporting. The project centralises these activities around one operational database.')
